# XSH atomic_init(), and the ATOMIC_VAR_INIT macro of <stdatomic.h>
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Objects are filled with junk bytes first, so that atomic_init() has to
# supply the value (and any other state) itself.

assertion  XSH.atomic_init.001
anchor     functions/atomic_init.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       After atomic_init(&obj, v) on an automatic atomic object whose
           storage held junk, the object holds v (read plainly and with
           atomic_load()), for atomic_bool and every atomic integer type with
           the values 0, 1, minimum and maximum; also the page's example
           (atomic_int guide; atomic_init(&guide, 42)).
test       t/001-init-automatic.c

assertion  XSH.atomic_init.002
anchor     functions/atomic_init.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       An atomic object in malloc()ed memory that held junk, after
           atomic_init(), supports atomic_load(), atomic_fetch_add(),
           atomic_exchange(), atomic_compare_exchange_strong() and
           atomic_store() with the expected results, for every atomic
           integer type but atomic_bool.
test       t/002-init-heap-then-use.c

assertion  XSH.atomic_init.003
anchor     functions/atomic_init.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       atomic_init() on atomic pointer objects (to int, a structure, a
           function; null included) makes them hold the pointer, and
           atomic_exchange() and atomic_load() then work on them.
test       t/003-init-pointer.c

assertion  XSH.atomic_init.004
anchor     basedefs/stdatomic.h.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       The macro ATOMIC_VAR_INIT(value) exists and initializes atomic
           objects of automatic and static duration (int, bool, unsigned long
           long, char, long, unsigned int, int pointer) to the value.
note       The macro belongs to <stdatomic.h> (obsolescent, shaded OB); it is
           tested here because it is an initializer of atomic objects like
           atomic_init().
test       t/004-var-init.c
